Description: Implements Adaptive Piecewise Local Interpretable
    Model-Agnostic Explanations (AP-LIME) and its second-order
    interaction extension (AP2-LIME) for interpreting predictions
    from machine learning models. The methods replace the
    conventional locally weighted linear surrogate in LIME with
    Multivariate Adaptive Regression Splines (MARS).
    AP-LIME uses additive piecewise-linear hinge functions,
    whereas AP2-LIME allows pairwise interactions between
    hinge functions. The package generates proximity-weighted
    local explanations, estimates feature contributions,
    evaluates local surrogate fit, and assesses explanation
    stability across repeated runs. Stability is measured
    using the Variables Stability Index (VSI) and Coefficients
    Stability Index (CSI), including normal-theory and
    percentile bootstrap confidence intervals. MARS terms
    with the same predictors, hinge directions, and interaction
    structure are matched independently of knot locations.
    Coefficients within matched groups are summarized by
    their arithmetic mean, while the original knot thresholds
    remain available for inspection. The MARS-based local explanation 
    approach is discussed by Somuncuoglu and Purutcuoglu 
    (2027, ISBN:978-1-041-34431-5),
    "Explainable AI Approaches in Biomedical Signals:
    A Case Study with Pima Indians Diabetes Dataset",
    in "Biomedical Data Science: A Focus on Signaling",
    CRC Press.
